<title>JAPAN: Tokyo Senpaku shares rise on EPS increase.</title>
<headline>Tokyo Senpaku shares rise on EPS increase.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in ship operator Tokyo Senpaku Kaisha Ltd rose in active morning trade on Monday, supported by a rise in the firm's earnings per share (EPS) for the interim period, traders said.</p>
<p>The share price was up 50 yen at 555 yen by the end of the morning session, with volume at 496,000 shares.</p>
<p>Tokyo Senpaku said on Friday that its EPS was 15.03 yen in the six months to September 30, 1996, up from 4.49 yen in the same period a year ago.</p>
</text>
